  "outro": {
    "id": "outro",
    "x": 20,
    "y": 660,
    "width": 280,
    "height": 330,
    "css": "font-size: 19px;",
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "clickable": false,
    "layer": -1,
    "z": 10,
    "html": "Every button writes one <b>dragLimit</b> onto the piece and puts it back in the middle of the new area.<br><br>\n\nIn Edit Widgets, select the piece and look at Position > Drag limits: the same four sides and conditions are there as fields, and &quotShow on board&quot shades the whole area for you while you type it."
  },
  "language": {
    "id": "language",
    "x": 1310,
    "y": 68,
    "width": 280,
    "height": 250,
    "css": "font-size: 19px;",
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "clickable": false,
    "layer": -1,
    "z": 10,
    "html": "The math is the one <b>var</b> uses, so a formula reads the same in both: + - * / % ^ and brackets, abs, sqrt, hypot, min, max, sin, cos, tan and atan2 in degrees, PI. A bare name is a property of the widget: width, height, anything your game puts on it. ${PROPERTY name OF id} reads another widget's. && and || combine within one line."
  },
